---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Display from '../components/Display.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { releases, formatBytes } from '../data/releases';
const release = releases.frame;
---
<Base title="Hearthboard Frame · A frame for your everyday" description="Give a compatible Android photo frame a new purpose with Hearthboard Frame. Signed APK downloads, frame compatibility, sideloading guides, and pairing help.">
<section class="container page-hero"><div><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Displays</a><span>/</span><span>Frame</span></div><div class="eyebrow">A FRAME FOR YOUR EVERYDAY</div><h1>Hearthboard<br />Frame<span style="color:#a78c69">.</span></h1><p class="lead">More than a place for photos. Bring your day together on a compatible Android frame, with Hearthboard on your iPhone.</p><div class="intro-badges"><span class="pill">Android photo frames</span><span class="pill">Beta</span><span class="pill">No Google Play Services required</span></div><div class="button-row"><a class="button primary" href="#download">{release ? 'Download Frame' : 'Download availability'} <Icon name="download" size={18}/></a><a class="text-link" href="/docs/frame-compatibility/">Check your frame <Icon name="arrow" size={17}/></a></div></div><div class="product-art frame-art"><Display kind="frame"/><span class="art-tag">ILLUSTRATIVE DASHBOARD · SAMPLE CONTENT</span></div></section>
<section class="content-section"><div class="container two-col"><div><div class="eyebrow">FIRST, FIND YOUR FIT</div><h2 style="margin-top:15px">Android on the inside.<br />Hearthboard on the outside.</h2><p class="prose">The app targets Android 6.0 and newer. Whether you can install it depends on your frame's firmware, launcher, and access to Android settings.</p><div class="notice"><strong>Check before buying a frame</strong><p>Matching a brand name or model label isn't enough. The same frame can ship with different firmware. Verify APK installation access and the exact firmware first.</p></div><a class="text-link" href="/docs/frame-compatibility/">Read the compatibility guide <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a></div><div><table class="spec-table"><caption class="eyebrow" style="text-align:left;padding-bottom:12px">WHAT TO CHECK</caption><tbody><tr><th>Android</th><td>6.0 / API 23 or newer is the current app target</td></tr><tr><th>Installation</th><td>Access to APK installation, Files, a browser, or ADB</td></tr><tr><th>Network</th><td>Same home network as your iPhone for initial discovery</td></tr><tr><th>Hardware features</th><td>Brightness, motion, and reboot support vary by device</td></tr><tr><th>Known development frame</th><td>PF1007L · specific Android 6 firmware, with device-specific provisioning</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section>
<section class="content-section"><div class="container two-col"><div><div class="eyebrow">A NEW PLACE FOR YOUR DAY</div><h2 style="margin-top:15px">Install. Pair.<br />Make yourself at home.</h2><ol class="setup-steps"><li><strong>Check compatibility</strong>Confirm your frame can install APKs. Stock photo-frame software may hide Android settings.</li><li><strong>Install the signed app</strong>Download on the frame, or copy the APK using microSD or USB. Allow installation from the source you use.</li><li><strong>Pair with your iPhone</strong>Open Frame, join your home network, and pair in Hearthboard. Compare and confirm the six digits on both screens.</li><li><strong>Settle it in</strong>Choose your widgets. Set Hearthboard as the home app where supported, then check brightness and reboot behavior.</li></ol><a class="text-link" href="/docs/frame-install/">Step-by-step instructions <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a></div><div class="install-panel" id="download"><div class="eyebrow">THE ANDROID APP</div><h3 style="margin-top:12px">Get Hearthboard Frame.</h3>{release ? <><p class="status-line">{release.channel === 'beta' ? 'Public beta' : 'Stable release'} · {release.version}</p><p class="small">A signed APK for compatible Android frames. Install it directly on your frame.</p><a class="button primary" href={release.downloadURL}>Download APK <Icon name="download" size={18}/></a><p class="download-meta">{formatBytes(release.size)} · Android API {release.minSdk}+ · Version code {release.versionCode}</p><p class="download-meta">SHA-256: <code>{release.sha256}</code></p><a class="privacy-link" href="/releases/">Release notes & previous versions</a></> : <><div class="notice"><strong>The first public beta is being prepared</strong><p>The signed APK will appear here when the release is verified. There is no public Android download yet.</p></div><a class="button outline" href="/docs/frame-install/">Read the installation guide <Icon name="book" size={17}/></a><p class="release-state">Check <a class="privacy-link" href="/releases/">Downloads & releases</a> for availability.</p></>}<div class="notice warning"><strong>Already have a development build?</strong><p>Public and debug builds can use different package IDs and signing keys. Read the update guide before replacing an existing installation.</p></div><a class="privacy-link" href="/docs/updates/">How installation & updates work</a></div></div></section>
<section class="container content-section"><h2>A little help for the little things.</h2><div class="link-grid"><a class="guide-card" href="/docs/frame-install/"><span class="guide-icon"><Icon name="download" size={23}/></span><h3>Your first installation</h3><p>APK installation, unknown sources, and your first pairing.</p><span class="text-link">Read the guide <Icon name="arrow" size={15}/></span></a><a class="guide-card" href="/docs/frame-daily-use/"><span class="guide-icon"><Icon name="sun" size={23}/></span><h3>Make it feel at home</h3><p>Home app, brightness, sleep, and useful device settings.</p><span class="text-link">Read the guide <Icon name="arrow" size={15}/></span></a><a class="guide-card" href="/docs/troubleshooting/"><span class="guide-icon"><Icon name="info" size={23}/></span><h3>When something needs a hand</h3><p>Discovery, pairing, missing feeds, and collecting useful details.</p><span class="text-link">Get some help <Icon name="arrow" size={15}/></span></a></div></section>
</Base>
